<Legal
  lang="en"
  path="/datenschutz/"
  title="Privacy policy | Janis Schubert"
  description="How shubrt.me handles personal data: hosting, contact form, no cookies, no tracking."
>
  <h1>Privacy policy</h1>

  <h2>Controller</h2>
  <address>
    Janis Schubert Sales<br />
    Hauptstraße 15<br />
    55286 Sulzheim<br />
    Germany
  </address>
  <p>Email: <a href="mailto:contact@shubrt.me">contact@shubrt.me</a></p>

  <h2>Hosting and delivery</h2>
  <p>
    Cloudflare, Inc. (USA) hosts and delivers this website. On every visit Cloudflare processes
    technical connection data, including IP address, time, requested URL and browser details.
    Without this data the site can be neither delivered nor protected against attacks. The legal
    basis is Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR, the legitimate interest being secure delivery of the website.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact form</h2>
  <p>
    The form transmits name, email address and the page language, plus an optional topic and
    message. This data goes by email via Cloudflare to a Gmail inbox at Google. The website itself
    stores none of it. To catch spam the server checks a hidden field and the time since the page
    loaded, and stores neither.
  </p>
  <p>
    The purpose is to answer the inquiry. The legal basis is Art. 6(1)(b) GDPR where the inquiry
    concerns a contract or pre-contractual steps, otherwise Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR. The legitimate
    interest is then to answer inquiries.
  </p>
  <p>
    Emails stay in the inbox as long as handling the inquiry requires it or statutory retention
    duties apply. Cloudflare forwards emails sent to the address above to this inbox, where the
    same rule applies. A reply needs a name and an email address. Everything else is voluntary.
  </p>

  <h2>No cookies, no tracking</h2>
  <p>
    This website sets no cookies and uses no analytics or tracking services. It loads no third-party
    fonts or embedded content. No automated decision-making takes place.
  </p>

  <h2>Transfers to the USA</h2>
  <p>
    Cloudflare and Google are based in the USA or have a US parent company, so data may reach the
    USA. The basis is the European Commission's adequacy decision on the EU-US Data Privacy Framework
    (Art. 45 GDPR), where the provider is certified under it.
  </p>

  <h2>Rights</h2>
  <p>
    Data subjects have the right of access (Art. 15 GDPR), rectification (Art. 16), erasure (Art.
    17), restriction of processing (Art. 18) and data portability (Art. 20). They may object to
    processing under Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR (Art. 21). An email to the address above is enough.
  </p>
  <p>
    They also have the right to lodge a complaint with a supervisory authority (Art. 77 GDPR). The
    competent authority is the State Commissioner for Data Protection and Freedom of Information of
    Rhineland-Palatinate (LfDI), <a href="https://www.datenschutz.rlp.de/">datenschutz.rlp.de</a>.
  </p>

  <p>Last updated: November 2026</p>
</Legal>
